Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_databases
Fix: Turn ssl on, with a certificate the clients check.
References: postgresql.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 3.10; NIST SC-8; ISO 5.14, 8.24

PostgreSQL takes unencrypted connections from the network: ssl is off
while it listens past localhost. Passwords and data cross the wire
readable to anyone on it.
